From 841fe4609a7da2722010cbaef969eafca1c90c09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quince <quinceroms@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:50:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] release: Disable native app zygote prototype flags in cp2a

The native app zygote prototype (android.os.native_app_zygote + android.os.native_framework_prototype) is unreliable across kernels. On kernels without CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE (e.g. 4.14) the native app zygote child aborts during startup, killing every Chromium-based browser and WebView. On a device running kernel 5.10.252 - where the capability is available - the native path still fails even after the capability-loop guard and tmpfs sepolicy fixes, so the prototype is broken beyond the capability issue.

Disabling both flags routes all isolated services through the mature Java app zygote path, which works on every kernel. Both flags are READ_ONLY, so DISABLED is baked in as a compile-time constant and the ActiveServices gate(Flags.nativeAppZygote() && r.mIsNativeIsolated) can never select the native path.

Change-Id: I3350479062ad45be74d9b2ec97d94361d2360ff3
Signed-off-by: Quince <quinceroms@gmail.com>

diff --git a/release/aconfig/cp2a/android.os/native_app_zygote_flag_values.textproto b/release/aconfig/cp2a/android.os/native_app_zygote_flag_values.textproto
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8777123
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/aconfig/cp2a/android.os/native_app_zygote_flag_values.textproto
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+flag_value {
+  package: "android.os"
+  name: "native_app_zygote"
+  state: DISABLED
+  permission: READ_ONLY
+}
diff --git a/release/aconfig/cp2a/android.os/native_framework_prototype_flag_values.textproto b/release/aconfig/cp2a/android.os/native_framework_prototype_flag_values.textproto
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..25a32c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/aconfig/cp2a/android.os/native_framework_prototype_flag_values.textproto
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+flag_value {
+  package: "android.os"
+  name: "native_framework_prototype"
+  state: DISABLED
+  permission: READ_ONLY
+}
-- 
